<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.3.3: Solving Equations Using Substitution</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00409</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.3.3: Solving Equations Using Substitution</md:title>
    <md:uuid>662dc060-0315-42d0-9d29-6c073fa9339d</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Solve each system without graphing.</para>

<para>Use this system of equations to answer questions 1 – 3.</para>
<para><quote>\( \begin{cases} x + 2y = 8 \\x = -5 \end{cases} \)</quote></para><para>Here are the four systems of equations you saw in the previous exercise. Solve each system. Then, check your solutions by substituting them into the original equations to see if the equations are true.
</para>

<section class="check-understanding"><title>Activity</title><exercise id="_33fba438-5fcc-4669-afb7-7f659afd783b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>What is the \(x\) value?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 6</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is 6.</para></solution></exercise></section><!-- END ACTIVITY INPUT 1 TRY -->
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="b552fe1d-7d76-4a1e-b0a4-b65888a5a287" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>What is the \(y\) value?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 2</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is 2.</para></solution></exercise></section><!-- END ACTIVITY INPUT 1 TRY -->
<!-- BEGIN CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->

<!--Q3-->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Explain your solution.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
  
  <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}
    5x-2y&amp;=&amp;26
    \\ 5(y+4)-2y&amp;=&amp;26
    \\ 5y+20-2y&amp;=&amp;26
    \\ 3y+20&amp;=&amp;26
    \\ 3y&amp;=&amp;6
    \\ y&amp;=&amp;=2
    \\ \end{array}\)</para>
  
  <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  
  
  
  <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}
    \\ 2+4&amp;=&amp;x
    \\ 6&amp;=&amp;x
    \\ \end{array}\)</para>
  
  <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  
  
  
  <!--BEGIN SIDE BY SIDE EQUATIONSS-->
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcr}
    5(6)-2(2)=26 &amp;   &amp; \\
    30-4\overset?=26 &amp;   &amp; 2+4\overset?=6 \\
    26=26\checkmark &amp;   &amp; 6=6\checkmark
    \end{array}\)</para>
  
  <!--END SIDE BY SIDE EQUATIONS -->

</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->

<!-- END CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->

<para>Use this system of equations to answer 4 - 6.</para>
<para><quote>\( \begin{cases} 2m - 2p = -6\\ p = 2m + 10 \end{cases} \)</quote></para><section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="c58b42e1-2db3-413d-9503-72c0745a55a7" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>What is the \(m\) value?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! -7</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is -7.</para></solution></exercise></section><!-- END ACTIVITY INPUT 1 TRY -->
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="_6f943379-eb55-44a5-9c30-69d7b46fa41d" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>What is the \(p\) value?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! -4</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is -4.</para></solution></exercise></section><!-- END ACTIVITY INPUT 1 TRY -->
<!-- BEGIN CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->

<!--Q6-->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Explain your solution.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
  
  <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}
    2m-2p&amp;=&amp;-6
    \\ 2m-2(2m+10)&amp;=&amp;-6
    \\ 2m-4m-20&amp;=&amp;-6
    \\ -2m-20&amp;=&amp;-6
    \\ -2m&amp;=&amp;14
    \\ m&amp;=&amp;-7
    \\ \end{array}\)</para>
  
  <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  
  
  
  <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}
    p&amp;=&amp;2m+10
    \\ p&amp;=&amp;2(-7)+10
    \\ p&amp;=&amp;-14+10
    \\ p&amp;=&amp;-4
    \\ \end{array}\)</para>
  
  <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  
  
  
  <!--BEGIN SIDE BY SIDE EQUATIONSS-->
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcr}
    2(-7)-2(-4)=-6 &amp;   &amp; -4=2(-7)+10\\
    -14+8\overset?=-6 &amp;   &amp; -4\overset?=(-14)+10 \\
    -6=-6\checkmark &amp;   &amp; -4=-4\checkmark
    \end{array}\)</para>
  
  <!--END SIDE BY SIDE EQUATIONS -->

</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->

<!-- END CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->

<para>Use this system of equations to answer 7 - 9.</para>
<para><quote>\( \begin{cases} 2d = 8f \\ 18 - 4f = 2d \end{cases} \)</quote></para><section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="_8ce6e32e-2f46-4628-ba5b-daa3c7b9ccb0" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>What is the \(d\) value?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 6</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is 6.</para></solution></exercise></section><!-- END ACTIVITY INPUT 1 TRY -->
<!-- BEGIN TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->

<!--Q8-->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the \(f\) value?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    
    <para> \(\frac32\)</para>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!-- END TEXT ENTRY WITH REVEAL -->
<!-- BEGIN CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->

<!--Q9-->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Explain your solution.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
  
  <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}
    2d&amp;=&amp;8f
    \\ d&amp;=&amp;4f
    \\ \end{array}\)</para>
  
  <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  
  
  
  <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}
    18-4f&amp;=&amp;2d
    \\ 18-4f&amp;=&amp;2(4f)
    \\ 18-4f&amp;=&amp;8f
    \\ 18&amp;=&amp;12f
    \\ \frac{18}{12}&amp;=&amp;f
    \\ \frac32&amp;=&amp;f
    \\ \end{array}\)</para>
  
  <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  
  
  
  <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}
    2d&amp;=&amp;8(\frac32)
    \\ 2d&amp;=&amp;12
    \\ d&amp;=&amp;6
    \\ \end{array}\)</para>
  
  <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  
  
  
  <!--BEGIN SIDE BY SIDE EQUATIONSS-->
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcr}
    &amp;   &amp; 18-4f=2d \\
    2d=8f &amp;   &amp; 18-4(\frac32)=2(6) \\
    2(6)=8(\frac32) &amp;   &amp; 18-(2)(3)=12 \\
    12\overset?=(4)(3) &amp;   &amp; 18-6=12 \\
    12=12\checkmark &amp;   &amp; 12=12\checkmark
    \end{array}\)</para>
  
  <!--END SIDE BY SIDE EQUATIONS -->

</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->

<!-- END CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->
<para>Use this system of equations to answer 10 - 12.</para>
<para><quote>\( \begin{cases} w + \frac17z = 4 \\ z = 3w -2 \end{cases} \)</quote></para><section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="_7b3cebfa-349d-41c3-b87b-c80149441ef6" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>What is the \(w\) value?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 3</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is 3</para></solution></exercise></section><!-- END ACTIVITY INPUT 1 TRY -->
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="d4deb8ba-7cb4-4b57-8d73-8e7b37797294" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>What is the \(z\) value?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 7</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is 7.</para></solution></exercise></section><!-- END ACTIVITY INPUT 1 TRY -->
<!-- BEGIN CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->

<!--Q12-->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Explain your solution.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
  
  <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}
    w+\frac17z&amp;=&amp;4
    \\ w+\frac17(3w-2)&amp;=&amp;4
    \\ 7w+3w-2&amp;=&amp;28
    \\ 10w-2&amp;=&amp;28
    \\ 10w&amp;=&amp;30
    \\ w&amp;=&amp;3
    \\ \end{array}\)</para>
  
  <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  
  
  
  <!--BEGIN ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcl}
    z&amp;=&amp;3w-2
    \\ z&amp;=&amp;3(3)-2
    \\ z&amp;=&amp;9-2
    \\ z&amp;=&amp;7
    \\ \end{array}\)</para>
  
  <!--END ALIGN TO EQUALS -->
  
  
  
  <!--BEGIN SIDE BY SIDE EQUATIONSS-->
  
  <para>\(\begin{array}{rcr}
    w+\frac17z=4 &amp;   &amp; z=3w-2 \\
    3+\frac17(7)=4 &amp;   &amp; 7=3(3)-2 \\
    3+1\overset?=1=4 &amp;   &amp; 7\overset?=1=9-2 \\
    4=4 \checkmark &amp;   &amp; 7=7 \checkmark \\
    \end{array}\)</para>
  
  <!--END SIDE BY SIDE EQUATIONS -->

</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->

<!-- END CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->
<para>Solve this system with four equations.</para>
<para>Use this system of equations to answer questions 1 – 4.</para>
<para><quote>\( \begin{cases}3 x + 2y - z + 5w= 20 \\ y = 2z-3w\\ z=w+1 \\ 2w=8 \end{cases} \)</quote></para><section class="check-understanding"><title>Extending Your Thinking</title><exercise id="e7e035a3-3b18-46c1-97f2-b2ade9bcaaf2" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>What is the \(x\) value?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 3</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is 3.</para></solution></exercise></section><!-- END ACTIVITY INPUT 1 TRY -->
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="ee8d167f-4d01-41f8-a3e7-0ebee296816b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>What is the \(y\) value?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! -2</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is -2.</para></solution></exercise></section><!-- END ACTIVITY INPUT 1 TRY -->
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="fec9bd23-0a98-4791-8846-fa412c54fe4c" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>What is the \(z\) value?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 5</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is 5.</para></solution></exercise></section><!-- END ACTIVITY INPUT 1 TRY -->
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise id="_06683489-101e-452e-935f-97b24a2fd78b" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>What is the \(w\) value?</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! 4</para><para>Nice try! The correct answer is 4.</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
